out.push(note('Teacher\'s note. Four faults to watch, and the remedy for each. First, the straw version. Every learner\'s first attempt is the case they can answer, and the diagnostic question is how long it would take to refute: two sentences means it is nobody\'s case. The remedy is the reframing — what would its holder write with three days and your documents — and the thing to insist on is that the documents are the opponent\'s, which is why the strong version so often contains a distinction the holder could not have made. And separate believing a case from thinking it sufficient, because a learner who thinks honesty requires disbelief will write something they can disbelieve. Second, the leak. Learners announce objectivity and then leak in four places: adjectives, the ordering of a list, a repeated disclaimer, and the attribution verb. Teach the two-step on leaning words rather than simple deletion — find the word, ask what it was being used to say, and say that instead, because about two thirds of the time there is a fact underneath and the paper gains. On ordering, the remedy is declaration and not rearrangement: every order is a judgement and the only fix is to state the principle. Third, the mood dressed as a condition. "I would need to be convinced" cannot be satisfied, tested or shown to have been met, and a class will offer it without any intention of obstructing. The question that does the work is "above what figure", and it usually sends them to a calculation they have never done; expect the number to surprise them, and in about a third of cases to be lower than they assumed, which changes their own position before anybody argues. Then make them ask the holder for the harder condition — not what would convince you but what would make you abandon it — because that one costs its author something and is therefore worth more. Fourth, and this is the one with the longest reach: the third question of the recognition test. Learners will ask whether the paper is the holder\'s and whether there is anything in it they would not say, and then stop, because a paper that has been read aloud looks finished. Stage the silence once in class — have the reader say "then I think we are finished" and wait — and the thing that comes out will be in no document and will be half the proposer\'s reason. Two notes on 16.7. The mechanism for choosing the writer is about how lenders read and not about fairness, and teaching it as fairness loses it: a believer\'s paper gets read for the omission, and the omission is always there. And Mr Ayoub\'s closing line matters more than it looks — that she writes the next paper too, whichever way the count goes — because a practice that depends on one person\'s willingness dies with their patience, and a practice that is simply how the company writes to its bank does not.'));

if (require.main === module) L.build(out, process.argv[2], 'Proactive Business English B2 · Book 2 · Syria Edition · Unit 16 · Answer Key');
module.exports = out;
